B.a8c=new A.nA("Finger Millet (Ragi / Mandua / Kezhvaragu)","Ragi (Kannada/Hindi), Kezhvaragu (Tamil), Ragulu (Telugu)","Eleusine coracana","344 mg calcium per 100g (10x higher than rice/wheat), rich in polyphenols and slowly digestible starch.","Soak for 12 hours, sprout for 24 hours to trigger endogenous phytases, dry, and mill. Sprouting increases bioavailable iron and zinc by up to 300% while degrading phytate chelators.","Clinical trials show finger millet lowers glycemic index, delays gastric emptying, and significantly improves bone mineral density markers.")
B.a8b=new A.nA("Pearl Millet (Bajra / Kambu / Sajjalu)","Bajra (Hindi), Kambu (Tamil), Sajjalu (Telugu), Sajje (Kannada)","Pennisetum glaucum","High non-heme iron (8 mg/100g), high magnesium, rich in oleic and linoleic unsaturated fatty acids.","Due to high lipid content, milled bajra flour oxidizes rapidly. Grind fresh in small batches. Combine with vitamin C sources (lemon, tomato) to enhance iron absorption.","Regular consumption of biofortified pearl millet reverses iron deficiency and improves cognitive endurance in adolescents (p < 0.01).")
B.a8a=new A.nA("Foxtail Millet (Kangni / Thinai / Korra)","Kangni (Hindi), Thinai (Tamil), Korra (Telugu), Navane (Kannada)","Setaria italica","High dietary fiber (8-10%), low glycemic load, abundant thiamine (B1) and tryptophan.","Wash 2 times, soak for 4-6 hours, and cook with 1:2.5 water ratio as a direct rice replacement.","Significant improvements in fasting blood glucose and lipid profiles in individuals with type 2 diabetes consuming foxtail millet over 90 days.")
